{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CEFbh5P7MpHErTJYievdJ4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor â€” Productivity System for J.C. Liechty**\n\n- **It's a single-folder, stdlib-only personal productivity system** living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` â€” no database, no syncing, no external dependencies (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals). Plain markdown files are the source of truth.\n\n- **At its core it's a task/project manager.** It tracks tasks and projects across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored), driven by markdown files like `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, and `domains/*.md`.\n\n- **It ships two interfaces over the same logic:** `anchor_gui.py` (a persistent local web server on `http://localhost:8777`, run as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`, serving an interactive browser dashboard that writes markdown directly) and `anchor.py` (a CLI mirror that also generates a static `dashboard.html`).\n\n- **It includes a daily self-test** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`, scheduled 5 AM) that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, walks a synthetic task through all states, and writes a dated report â€” surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **It has grown an \"R&D Control Surface\" (v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4)** that turns each project's window into a cockpit for \"trio\"-driven R&D work (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). This adds: session-grouped history, cached/validated summaries, a Grass Catchers idea lane, pinned deliverables, real ConPTY interactive terminals with per-session git-worktree isolation, an engine toggle (Claude/Gemini), per-lane doc roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, and type-aware deliverable launches.\n\n- **The current branch (`foreman/rnd-surface-v4`) is the \"Project Cockpit\" build** â€” lane tiles with status lights, inline expanding panels (summary-over-terminal), flat dashboard rows, and Ghost World Labs branding (\"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"). Per the latest commit it's marked PROJECT DONE with the healthcheck green.\n\nThese are drawn from the project's `CLAUDE.md` and frozen North-Star/design docs; I haven't independently re-verified the code against each claim. Want me to spot-check any of them against the source?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24496,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24496},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d82e2d8c-5526-4eed-bcd4-eb66da54d3c1","uuid":"34b2ecf4-6df5-4ff3-90d6-4feec3d0e982","request_id":"req_011Cc1H5MWicJx6znZYzcQsr"}
